---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="SigScan Privacy Policy | James Tannahill"
  description="Privacy policy for the SigScan iOS app: what data the app handles and how it stays on your device."
  canonical="https://jamestannahill.com/sigscan/privacy"
>
  <div class="bg-white min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <h1 class="text-[28px] font-medium tracking-tight mb-2" style="color:#1a1a1a;">SigScan Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-[12px] mb-12" style="color:var(--color-muted);">Last updated: October 1, 2026</p>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">Overview</p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] mb-4" style="color:#444;">
          This Privacy Policy describes how the <strong>SigScan</strong> iOS application ("the App") handles
          information. SigScan is a utility for viewing the wireless environment around your own device. It has
          no user accounts, no advertising, no third-party analytics, and no tracking of any kind.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85]" style="color:#444;">
          The short version: your scans are stored on your device and nothing is collected about you. Scan data leaves your phone only when you ask the optional AI assistant a question, as described below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">Data the App Handles On-Device</p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] mb-4" style="color:#444;">
          To do its job, SigScan processes the following information locally on your iPhone:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] mb-4 pl-5 list-disc" style="color:#444;">
          <li>Bluetooth advertisements broadcast by nearby devices (names, manufacturer data, signal strength)</li>
          <li>NFC tag contents when you deliberately hold your phone against a tag</li>
          <li>Your current WiFi network details and devices advertising services on your local network</li>
          <li>Carrier and radio technology information from iOS</li>
          <li>Camera frames, used only to render the live augmented reality view; frames are never saved or transmitted</li>
          <li>Your GPS location, used only to stamp your own scan history so you can review it on a map</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85]" style="color:#444;">
          All of this is stored on your device using Apple's SwiftData framework. It is not uploaded to any
          server, except for the assistant summary described below when you ask a question, and it is included
          in your device backups only according to your own iOS backup settings.
          Deleting the App deletes this data. CSV export shares data only where you explicitly choose to send it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">The AI Assistant Feature</p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] mb-4" style="color:#444;">
          SigScan includes an optional assistant that answers questions about your scan results. When you type a
          question, the App sends your question to a server operated by the developer, which forwards it to
          Anthropic's Claude API and returns the answer. Along with your question, the App sends:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85] mb-4 pl-5 list-disc" style="color:#444;">
          <li>A summary of up to 20 scanned devices: make, model, signal type, category, chip maker, average signal strength, how many times each was seen, risk flags and the evidence for them, whether it appeared to be moving, and how many places it was logged</li>
          <li>Your last 30 scan events: device name, time and signal strength. In the current version of the App (1.3), each event also includes the coordinates where it was logged. We will update this policy when a version that omits coordinates is released</li>
          <li>No identifiers for your iPhone, no advertising identifiers and no account information (the App has no accounts)</li>
          <li>Queries are processed transiently to produce the answer and are not used to build any profile of you</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85]" style="color:#444;">
          If you never use the assistant, the App sends none of your scan data or location anywhere.
          Anthropic's handling of API traffic is described in the
          <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" class="underline hover:opacity-70" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">Anthropic Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">Data Collection</p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85]" style="color:#444;">
          The App collects no personal data. There are no accounts, no analytics SDKs, no advertising SDKs, no
          crash reporting services, and no tracking across apps or websites. The developer receives no information
          about you or your use of the App, other than the transient AI assistant queries described above and
          standard aggregate App Store statistics provided by Apple.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">Permissions</p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85]" style="color:#444;">
          SigScan requests Bluetooth, Camera, Location, NFC, HomeKit, and Local Network permissions solely to
          provide the features described above. Each permission is optional; the App degrades gracefully if a
          permission is declined. You can change permissions at any time in iOS Settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">Children</p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85]" style="color:#444;">
          The App is not directed at children and collects no personal data from anyone, including children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">Changes</p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85]" style="color:#444;">
          Material changes to this Policy will be reflected on this page with an updated date above. Continued use
          of the App after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised Policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">Contact</p>
        <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.85]" style="color:#444;">
          Questions about this Policy or the App can be sent via the
          <a href="/contact" class="underline hover:opacity-70" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">contact form</a>
          on this site. The App is available on the
          <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/sigscan-signal-radar/id6806315838" class="underline hover:opacity-70" style="color:var(--color-amber-text);">App Store</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
